# Cursor Rules Index

Rules live in `.cursor/rules/`. `alwaysApply: true` → every session; `globs` → when matching files are in context.

## Always applied (4)

| Rule | Scope |
|------|-------|
| `chatwoot-core.mdc` | MVP approach, naming, errors, commits, i18n (EN + fork pt_BR), branding |
| `chatwoot-dev-commands.mdc` | Setup, run, seed, lint, test, worktrees |
| `architecture.mdc` | Layers, access-control surfaces, anti-patterns, composition |
| `fork-workflow.mdc` | Branches, `custom/`, Enterprise-via-Custom, `spec/custom`, FORK markers |

## File-scoped (3)

| Rule | Globs |
|------|-------|
| `ruby-conventions.mdc` | `**/*.rb` |
| `vue-frontend.mdc` | `**/*.{vue,js,ts}` (incl. async membership gates) |
| `enterprise-edition.mdc` | `{app,enterprise,lib,config}/**/*.{rb,yml}` (fork extensions → `custom/`) |

## On demand (1)

| Rule | When |
|------|------|
| `pull-requests.mdc` | Opening or drafting a PR |

## Entry points

`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.windsurf/rules/chatwoot.md` — short indexes only; **edit rules here**.
